emmo:EMMO_0c576e13_4ee7_4f3d_bfe9_1614243df018 a owl:Class;
                                               rdfs:comment "A topological space with the property that each point has a neighborhood that is homeomorphic to an open subset of 1-dimensional Euclidean space."@en,
                                                            "One-dimensional manifolds include lines and circles, but not self-crossing curves. Two-dimensional manifolds are also called surfaces. Examples include the plane, the sphere, and the torus, and also the Klein bottle and real projective plane."@en;
