emmo:EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7 a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                               rdfs:comment "This relation is about two wholes that overlap, and whose intersection is an holistic part of both."@en,
                                                            "A relation between two holistic wholes that properly overlap, sharing one of their holistic parts."@en;
                                               rdfs:domain emmo:EMMO_1efe8b96_e006_4a33_bc9a_421406cbb9f0;
                                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/perspectives/holistic#>;
                                               rdfs:label "holisticOverlaps"@en;
                                               rdfs:range emmo:EMMO_1efe8b96_e006_4a33_bc9a_421406cbb9f0;
                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf emmo:EMMO_bcaddc91_a881_4c40_a102_562cbaf61c6c;
                                               skos:example """A man and the process of building a house.
The man is a whole that possesses an holistic temporal part which is an interval of six monts and represents a working period in his lifetime.
The process of building a house is a whole that possesses an holistic spatial part which is a builder.
The working period of the man and the builder participating the building process are the same individual, belonging both to a man lifetime and to a building holistic views.
In this sense, the man and the building process overcrosses. and the overlapping individual is represented differently in both holistic views."""@en;
                                               skos:prefLabel "holisticOverlaps"@en;
                                               emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A relation between two holistic wholes that properly overlap, sharing one of their holistic parts."@en;
                                               emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "This relation is about two wholes that overlap, and whose intersection is an holistic part of both."@en.
