emmo:EMMO_6fa330f7_3289_4228_81df_12ee8a9708ac a owl:Class;
                                               rdfs:comment "Process consisting of two steps: - first, the steel is heated in a quenching treatment to a temperature above Ac3 and then rapidly cooled in a liquid to produce a process-specific grain structure; - subsequently, the steel is heated to a specific temperature during tempering to set the desired property and cooled in air.";
