emmo:EMMO_74a75cf1_3418_4244_b43c_b5db94635d42 a owl:AsymmetricProperty,
                                                 owl:ObjectProperty,
                                                 owl:IrreflexiveProperty;
                                               rdfs:comment "The relation grouping all direct parthood relations used in the reductionistic perspective."@en,
                                                            """Direct parthood is the non transitive version of parthood enabling the establishment of hierarchy of granularities, starting with an entity and providing several tesselation levels according to specific criteria.
The criteria are implemented in specialised versions of the direct parthood relation (e.g., metrological direct part, XML format direct part).
The direct parts (tiles) and the tessellated entity (tessellation) are causally self connected (i.e., items), coherently with the concept behind the definition of the reductionistic perspective.""",
                                                            "This relation is not antitransitive, to enable partitioning of a causal structure with more than one tiling scheme (e.g. time and space partitioning)."@en;
                                               rdfs:domain emmo:EMMO_ee0466e4_780d_4236_8281_ace7ad3fc5d2;
                                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/perspectives/reductionistic#>;
                                               rdfs:label "hasDirectPart"@en;
                                               rdfs:range emmo:EMMO_9953c19f_ee33_4af8_be5e_dbf6d1e33581;
                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf emmo:EMMO_9380ab64_0363_4804_b13f_3a8a94119a76;
                                               skos:prefLabel "hasDirectPart"@en;
                                               emmo:EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13 """Direct parthood is the non transitive version of parthood enabling the establishment of hierarchy of granularities, starting with an entity and providing several tesselation levels according to specific criteria.
The criteria are implemented in specialised versions of the direct parthood relation (e.g., metrological direct part, XML format direct part).
The direct parts (tiles) and the tessellated entity (tessellation) are causally self connected (i.e., items), coherently with the concept behind the definition of the reductionistic perspective.""";
                                               emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "The relation grouping all direct parthood relations used in the reductionistic perspective."@en;
                                               emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "This relation is not antitransitive, to enable partitioning of a causal structure with more than one tiling scheme (e.g. time and space partitioning)."@en,
                                                                                              "This relation is a simple collector of all relations inverse functional direct parthoods that can be defined in specialised theories using reductionism.".
